※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4567
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4567 LANG_LIFETIME_NOT_DETERMINED

※ A lambda's lifetime name stands on its own parameters or on those of a
※ signature around it.  `⧖zz` is on neither, so what the answer would live for
※ is undecided -- and this one answers with its own local, which nothing could
※ make right.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup, impure]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let g := λ → &⧖zz u32:
        let n: u32 = 3u32
        &n
    if g()⌖ = 3u32: 0u6 else: 1u6
